Build and install the command-line tools correctly on Windows

nauty links all 51 of its tools with libtool, but none of them actually uses a
libtool library -- they are all built from plain object files, so libtool adds
nothing to the link. What it does add on Windows is a small stand-in program
that starts the real one. When building for Windows from Linux, libtool cannot
work out the paths that stand-in needs:

    libtool: error: Could not determine the host path corresponding to
    libtool: error:   '/prefix/lib:/prefix/bin'
    libtool: error: Continuing, but uninstalled executables may not work.

and the tools it leaves behind then fail to start. Link the tools with the
compiler directly, which is all they ever needed. -no-undefined goes too, as
that is a libtool setting for shared libraries.

Two related fixes:

  - The install step looks for the tools under the names they had while
    building, but Windows programs need a .exe on the end. Install them one at
    a time, taking whichever name is present and always ending up with .exe,
    and stop at the first failure -- a plain loop only reports whether its last
    step worked, so a tool that fails to install is otherwise skipped quietly
    and only noticed much later.

  - showg is the one tool that was already linked with the compiler rather than
    libtool, and it was the one tool that went missing from the Windows build.
    Link it the same way as all the others so there is only one path to get
    wrong.

Finally, take the shared library naming from configure rather than always
putting the version number in, so Windows gets libnauty.dll while every other
system keeps the name it has now.

--- a/makefile.in
+++ b/makefile.in
@@ -28,8 +28,8 @@
 top_builddir=.
 LIBTOOL=@LIBTOOL@
 LTC=${LIBTOOL} --mode=compile ${CCC} -c 
-LTL=${LIBTOOL} --mode=link ${CCC} ${CYGNOUN} -rpath ${DESTDIR}${libdir} -release ${RELEASE} ${LDFLAGS}
-LTP=${LIBTOOL} --mode=link ${CCC} ${CYGNOUN} ${LDFLAGS}
+LTL=${LIBTOOL} --mode=link ${CCC} ${CYGNOUN} -rpath ${DESTDIR}${libdir} @libversionflag@ ${LDFLAGS}
+LTP=${CCC} ${LDFLAGS}
 CCOBJ=${LTC} -o $@
 
 INSTALL=@INSTALL@
@@ -770,7 +770,7 @@
 	${LTP} -o bliss2dre bliss2dre.c gtools${XO} ${XNAUTYO}
 
 showg : showg.c
-	${CCC} -o showg showg.c ${LDFLAGS}
+	${LTP} -o showg showg.c
 
 readg : showg
 	echo "*** readg is now called showg ***"
@@ -1009,7 +1009,10 @@
 
 install : all ${GLIBS}
 	${MKDIR_P} ${DESTDIR}${bindir} ${DESTDIR}${includedir} ${DESTDIR}${libdir} ${DESTDIR}${pkgconfigdir}
-	${INSTALL} ${GTOOLS} ${DESTDIR}${bindir}
+	for p in ${GTOOLS} ; do \
+	   if [ -f $$p${EXEEXT} ] ; then f=$$p${EXEEXT} ; else f=$$p ; fi ; \
+	   ${INSTALL} $$f ${DESTDIR}${bindir}/$$p${EXEEXT} || exit 1 ; \
+	done
 	${INSTALL_DATA} ${GTOOLSH} nausha.h ${DESTDIR}${includedir}
 	${LIBTOOL} --mode=install ${INSTALL} ${GLIBS} ${DESTDIR}${libdir}
 	${LIBTOOL} --mode=finish ${DESTDIR}${libdir}
